**D/A is not suitable.** Under D/A the buyer receives the title documents just by **accepting a time draft**, takes the goods, and pays only later. Documentary collections give **no bank guarantee of payment**. The slides say a seller should agree to documentary collection only if:

- there is **no doubt** about the buyer's ability and willingness to pay;
- the buyer's country is **politically, economically and legally stable**;
- there are **no exchange restrictions**;
- the goods are easily marketable.

At least the first three conditions fail here.

**Recommendation: cash-in-advance (T/T in advance)** or, if the buyer cannot accept that, an **irrevocable L/C, preferably confirmed** by a bank in a safer country. The slide criteria for cash-in-advance all apply: the importer is a **new customer** with no operating history; its **creditworthiness is unverifiable**; and the **political and commercial risks of the importer's country are very high**. *[EXT – Trade Finance Guide]* On the exporter's risk ladder, cash-in-advance and L/C (confirmed > unconfirmed) are lower risk than D/P and D/A.

**Cash-in-advance (T/T payment in advance).** The buyer remits first and the exporter ships last. The slide criteria for using cash-in-advance all apply:

- the importer is a **new customer**;
- its **creditworthiness is unverifiable**;
- the **political and commercial risks** of the importer's country are **very high**;
- the product is **unique and in heavy demand**, so the buyer is likely to accept.

scenario:
**Viet Bamboo Furniture** sells furniture to a US buyer **CIP Chicago, USA – Incoterms® 2020**. The invoice value is **USD 150,000**. The L/C (subject to UCP 600) requires:

> *“Insurance policy or certificate in duplicate, covering Institute Cargo Clauses (A) for 110% of the invoice value, claims payable in the USA.”*

The goods were handed to the first carrier on **5 June** (transport document date). The beneficiary presents:

- a **cover note issued by an insurance broker**;
- dated **8 June**;
- for **USD 150,000**;
- covering **ICC (C)**;
- **one** original.
